{"name":"Dove Grey","hex":"#6d6c6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dove grey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A medium grey colour with a slight tint of pink or blue, like that of a dove."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a medium grey colour with a slight tint of pink or blue, like that of a dove."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dove_grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Columbidae","blocks":[{"text":"Columbidae is a bird family consisting of doves and pigeons. It is the only family in the order Columbiformes. These are stout-bodied birds with small heads, relatively short necks and slender bills that in some species feature fleshy ceres. They feed largely on plant matter, feeding on seeds (granivory), fruit (frugivory), and foliage (folivory)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Treron_vernans_male_-_Kent_Ridge_Park.jpg/330px-Treron_vernans_male_-_Kent_Ridge_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbidae","wikidata":"Q10856"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Speckled_pigeon_%28Columba_guinea_guinea%29.jpg/500px-Speckled_pigeon_%28Columba_guinea_guinea%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Speckled_pigeon_%28Columba_guinea_guinea%29.jpg/1280px-Speckle